{"ref":"BDB, אִטִּי","hw":"אִטִּי","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">אִטִּי</span> Ol. <span dir=\"rtl\"></span><sup>412</sup>]</big>  <strong>n.m. mutterer</strong>, pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">אִטִּים</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 19:3\" href=\"/Isaiah.19.3\">Is 19:3</a> <em>mutterers</em> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">אֹבוֹת</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">יִדְּעֹנִים</span>) i.e. either ventriloquists or whisperers of charms (cf. <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 8:19\" href=\"/Isaiah.8.19\">8:19</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 29:4\" href=\"/Isaiah.29.4\">29:4</a>).","next":"BDB, אַט²","prev":"BDB, אטט"}